# EF Core SQLite sample database (created at runtime by samples/Rask.Example.EfCore)
raskExampleCatalog.db
raskExampleCatalog.db-shm
raskExampleCatalog.db-wal

# What a Rask app leaves beside itself when it runs. Every battery is on by default now, so ANY app
# that starts — a sample, a scaffolded project under test — creates its database, its log store, its
# mail pickup directory and its snapshot directory.
#
# A GLOB, because the per-name list this replaces claimed not to be one and was: it named app.db and
# logs.db, so samples/Rask.Example.Auth/auth-sample.db and the WasmCookie host's own database were
# never ignored and got COMMITTED. That is worse than clutter — those samples build their schema with
# EnsureCreated, which does nothing to a database that already exists, so the committed file froze the
# schema and every battery table added afterwards was silently missing. It surfaced as a browser
# journey dying on "Cannot create a DbSet for 'QueuedMail'" long after the table was added.
#
# Verified against `git ls-files` that this swallows nothing else tracked.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
mail-pickup/
snapshots/

# Coverage
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info

# Claude Code
.claude/settings.local.json

# Linked git worktrees created by tooling live INSIDE the repo, so without this an IDE opened on the repo
# root indexes a complete second copy of the framework per worktree. Every component type then exists
# N times over, the generator injects its chain entries into each copy, and a bare `Div` stops resolving
# to an entry — CS0119 on essentially every file, with nothing wrong in the code itself.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Other
*.swp
*.bak
*.cache
# Rask.Cache is a source package, not a build artifact — but its directory name matches the *.cache glob
# above on case-insensitive filesystems, which would ignore the whole package. Re-include it (its own
# bin/obj build output is still ignored by the [Bb]in/ and [Oo]bj/ rules, and *.cache files within still match).
!src/Rask.Cache/
*.dbmdl
*.dbproj.schemaview
*.publishsettings
publish/
PublishProfiles/
*.[Pp]ublish.xml

# Derived favicon — copied from assets/favicon.svg by example csproj targets.
Rask.Example.Server/wwwroot/favicon.svg
Rask.Example.Wasm.Host/wwwroot/

# Generated MSBuild task assembly — built by Rask.Wasm.Tasks and copied here on every
# build (see CopyTaskAssemblyToRaskWasmBuild). Its MVID/timestamp/PDB-hash differ per
# build environment, so committing it made it perpetually dirty in git.
src/Rask.Wasm/build/Rask.Wasm.Tasks.dll
src/Rask.Spa.Hosting/build/Rask.Spa.Tasks.dll
src/Rask.Meta.Hosting/build/Rask.Spa.Tasks.dll
src/Rask.Tailwind/build/Rask.Tailwind.Tasks.dll
src/Rask.External/build/Rask.External.Tasks.dll
src/Rask.Core/build/Rask.TypeScript.Tasks.dll

# Ad-hoc SQLite load-harness runs (the committed reference lives in Baselines/).
benchmarks/Rask.Benchmarks.Sqlite/Results/

# The WASM browser bundles are build output: esbuild writes them from Browser/main.ts and
# Resources/*.ts. They lived in git while the build assembled them by pasting files together at
# `// @@RASK_*@@` markers, because the spliced result was the only readable form of the whole
# runtime. The TypeScript is that form now.
src/Rask.Wasm/Browser/main.js
src/Rask.Wasm/Browser/rask.wasm.js
src/Rask.Wasm/Browser/rask-sw.js

# Tailwind output. Rask.Tailwind compiles Styles/app.css into wwwroot/css/ at build, so the file in the
# tree is a build artifact: committing it means a stale stylesheet can be served by a checkout that never
# ran the build, and every build shows up as a diff.
**/wwwroot/css/app.css

# Island bundles. Vite writes them into wwwroot so the SDK publishes them with no publish target
# of its own — but they are build output, regenerated on every build, and the chunk names are hashed.
**/wwwroot/_rask/external/

# The tsconfig fragment Rask writes for the @rask/* prop-type mapping. Generated, never committed.
**/obj/rask-external/

# Written by WasmWatchAppFixture during the WASM hot-reload E2E and deleted afterwards. Tracking it
# makes every gate run delete a tracked file and leaves the sample with a permanent probe route.
samples/Rask.Example.Wasm/Features/HotReloadProbePage.cs
